- Ahmedabad, India, experiences comparable peak temperatures but adopted a different strategy.
- Ahmedabad''s Heat Action Plan, launched in 2013, relies primarily on early-warning systems, public cooling centers, and adjusted work schedules rather than infrastructure modifications.', $lyceon_json$[{"key":"A","text":"Phoenix, Arizona, recorded 53 consecutive days above 43 degrees Celsius in 2024, prompting the city to invest $147 million in reflective road coatings and shade structures to combat the extreme heat."},{"key":"B","text":"While Phoenix has committed $147 million to physical infrastructure changes such as reflective coatings and shade structures, Ahmedabad has tackled comparable heat through its Heat Action Plan, which emphasizes early-warning systems, cooling centers, and adjusted work schedules."},{"key":"C","text":"Ahmedabad's Heat Action Plan, launched in 2013, uses early-warning systems, public cooling centers, and adjusted work schedules to help residents cope with extreme temperatures in the Indian city."},{"key":"D","text":"Both Phoenix and Ahmedabad experience extreme heat, with Phoenix recording 53 consecutive days above 43 degrees Celsius in 2024 and Ahmedabad facing comparable peak temperatures each year."}]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, 'B', NULL, E'The goal is to present a contrast between two cities'' mitigation approaches. The choice beginning "While Phoenix has committed $147 million to physical infrastructure changes" accomplishes this by directly juxtaposing Phoenix''s infrastructure-focused strategy with Ahmedabad''s policy-and-behavioral approach in a single contrastive sentence using "while." The option beginning "Phoenix, Arizona, recorded 53 consecutive days" discusses only Phoenix''s situation and investment without mentioning Ahmedabad, so it fails to present any contrast between the two cities. The option beginning "Ahmedabad''s Heat Action Plan" describes only Ahmedabad''s strategy without referencing Phoenix''s approach, omitting the comparative element. The option beginning "Both Phoenix and Ahmedabad experience extreme heat" notes their shared problem but describes only the temperature conditions, not their differing mitigation strategies, so it establishes similarity rather than contrast.', $lyceon_json${"A":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"rhetorical_purpose_error"},"B":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"C":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"partial_reasoning"},"D":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"rhetorical_purpose_error"}}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, NULL, 'draft', 1, 80, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-19"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-19","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);
